From: pokeplatinum-3ds <noreply@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 08:00:00 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] The lower menu's two squares (SDK_PORT_3DS)

The two squares under the lower menu's buttons show the registered
items' icons (handed to the port: NitroPort_LowerMenuSetItem) and use
them. The first is the item on Y; the second the one that was on Y
before it: REGISTER in the bag moves the item that was on Y to the second
square, DESELECT takes an item off either. The second square's item is
the port's (its setting item2), not the save's; it's shown only while the
bag has it.

A tap on a square uses its item as Y does (RegisteredItem_PortUse: Y's
work with any item; sub_02069238 calls it with the registered one), the
field taking the press with its input (FieldInput's portItem2 for the
second). With the menu open the cursor goes onto the squares (Up and
Down round the column and the squares, Left and Right between them) and
A uses the item; tapped in the bag, the party, the trainer case or the
options page, those close and the item's used back in the field. The
squares are dimmed where Y does nothing (the Battle Tower's salon, the
Pal Park). Without the lower menu the bag registers as the DS's.
